Subject: [PATCH] headless: virtual monitors from the profile's display layout

In headless mode the browser creates one virtual monitor per entry in
the profile's screen.displays, with its bounds, work area, device pixel
ratio, label, primary and internal flags, and color depth.
window.screen, getScreenDetails(), window placement and fullscreen all
read these monitors through the normal display code. Sizes in the
profile are CSS pixels and are converted once. Headful windows keep the
real monitors.

